1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Lê belê em îro di vê rê de bi hev re cem xalo bi navê kesekî
ne, çend sal e vî karî dikin.
 
However, we are on this road together today with an uncle
whose name we know, he has been doing this job for several
years.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Li cem me li herêma Efrînê, her gundekî, kesek gundê xwe ji
yê din çêtir dizane.
 
With us in the Afrin region, in every village, a person
knows their own village better than anyone else.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Ez dixwazim hûn jî ji min re binivîsin, di kurdî de navê vê
çî ye, kî dizane çî ye ji min re binivîse.
 
I want you to write to me as well, what is this called in
Kurdish, whoever knows what it is, write to me.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Te elî ya.
 
Did you say Ali?

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Elî jî wekî bira ye. Elî li Heleb dimîne.
 
Ali is like a brother. Ali lives in Aleppo.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Dembaş temaşevanên me yên hêja, temaşevanên me yên ezîz.
Sibeh bixêr.
 
Good day to our valuable viewers, to our dear viewers. Good
morning.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Ez bi hêvî me hûn di nav xêr û xweşiyê de bin.
 
I hope you are in good health and happiness.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Îro teswîra me ne li gundan e, ne li Efrînê ye.
 
Today, our filming is not in the villages, nor in Afrin.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Teswîra me îro rihê Efrînê ye, wextê em ê bi hev re derbas
bikin.
 
Our filming today is the spirit of Afrin, we will spend time
together.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Niha êdî pir kes hene, sibê zû dest pê kirin.
 
Right now there are many people, they started early in the
morning.

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Lê em jî hatin zeytûnan.
 
But we also came to the olives.

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Em ê zeytûnan ji xwe re hişîn jêkin, ez im û kekê Elî ye.
 
We will pick green olives for ourselves, it's me and brother
Ali.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Û em hatin nav zeytûnan, perçeyê meta Elî ye.
 
And we came among the olive trees, it is Ali's aunt's land.

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Ev zeytûn jî li pişta gundê Selo dikeve.
 
These olives are located behind Selo village.

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Em ê zeytûnên hişîn jêkin, di vê vîdyoyê de jî em ê her wisa
bi hev re derbas bikin ka em ê zeytûnan çawa jêkin.
 
We will pick green olives, and in this video, we will spend
time together showing how we pick olives.

16
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Piştî wê em ê çayek xwe jî li çolê çêkin, li nav darê, em ê
çawa hazir bikin.
 
After that, we will also make our tea in the field, among
the trees, how we will prepare it.

17
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Û dîsa niha em ê qehweya xwe jî vexwin.
 
And again, now we will also drink our coffee.

18
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Em zeytûnên xwe jî jêkin û paşê em ê sekînin.
 
We will pick our olives and then we will rest.

19
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Ev hişîn wextî jêdikin, ne tenê teke, teqez gir jêke.
 
When they pick these green ones, not just any, make sure to
pick the big ones.

20
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Kê gotiye em nizanin zeytûnan jêkin? Berî me didan şan.
 
Who said we don't know how to pick olives? They used to show
us.

21
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Me çar-pênc çuwal dikişand.
 
We used to haul four or five sacks.

22
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Na em dizanin zeytûnan jî jêbikin, em ji Efrînê ne.
 
No, we know how to pick olives, we are from Afrin.

23
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Hinge tu şaleki rêxe, wê wextê.
 
Then you lay down a cloth, at that time.

24
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Balî xew pê tê, piştî baran barî, gelek weşiyan e erdê.
 
Pay attention, one gets sleepy, after it rained, many fell
to the ground.

25
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Wele ev darên we pir gir in.
 
By God, these trees of yours are very big.

26
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Lê na niha ev te tenê nikarî paqij bikî.
 
But no, now you cannot clean this alone.

27
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Ev hişîn bes têkê nav re ê gir jêke.
 
Just pick the big green ones from among them.

28
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Niha bi du-sê rojên din jî... li Efrînê mazot qut bûye.
 
Now in another two or three days... diesel has been cut off
in Afrin.

29
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Ev e sibê çend gundiyên me gotin, mazot tine ye.
 
This morning a few of our villagers said there is no diesel.

30
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Îhtîmal e em biftilin meşê...
 
It's likely we will return to walking...

31
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Îhtîmal e em biftilin meşê...
 
It's likely we will return to walking...

32
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Qet bes ev mazot jî qut bû, em nizanin em ê çawa herin
gundan.
 
It's enough that this diesel was cut off, we don't know how
we will go to the villages.

33
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Gundê me darîn jî gundekî dûr e.
 
Our wooden village is also a distant village.

34
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Yanî em ê nikaribin herin navçeya Bilbilê, çilo mazot ger
eke, mazot jî qut bûye.
 
I mean, we won't be able to go to the Bilbil district,
diesel is needed for that, and diesel has been cut off.

35
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Yanî me hazirî dikir ku em du teswîran pêçê bikin. Niha em
hazirî terik dikin em vîdyoyan tenê pêçê bikin.
 
I mean, we were preparing to record two videos. Now we are
abandoning the preparation, we are only recording videos.

36
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Dû re em çûn basît e... em mesewiran.
 
Then we went, it's simple... we film.

37
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Lê ez nizanim ku mazot jî tin e, an jî nabe, em ê çawa herin
gundan teswîr bikin.
 
But I don't know, if there's no diesel, or it's not
possible, how will we go to the villages to film.

38
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Fe wê maneyê jî, ma dixwest em vîdyoyan jî ji we re çêkin.
 
Therefore, we wanted to make videos for you too.

39
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Vê zeytûnê hişîn em ê jêkin û nika bixwin.
 
We will pick these green olives and eat them now.

40
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Her wext mak bez wek tê bîr û baweriyên qewmê gundî...
 
Always, the speed is like the memories and beliefs of the
village people...

41
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Xwedê bereketê bixwe... û bi qismet û nesîb ke.
 
May God bring blessings... and make it a destiny and a
portion.

42
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Ji ber ku her rizqek heta bi wî re qismet nebe nabe.
 
Because every sustenance doesn't happen until it is destined
for someone.

43
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:37,000
Xwedê ev rizq da me, bi qismet û nesîb be.
 
God gave us this sustenance, may it be a destiny and a
portion.

44
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Kê ji we dizane kî di vê vîdyoyê sêr dike, wekî çawa em
zeytûnan dikişînin.
 
Who among you knows who is watching this video, how we pull
the olives.

45
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Kesên li Efrînê dimînin...
 
The people who live in Afrin...

46
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Kî felle ye dixe xeberên min...
 
Who is a Christian (farmer), putting words in my mouth...

47
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Kî felle ye? Ma em hemû... Kî emel e dixe xeberên min.
 
Who is a Christian? Are we all... Who is a worker, putting
words in my mouth.

48
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Elî li Heleb maye, nizane.
 
Ali stayed in Aleppo, he doesn't know.

49
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Xwedêke em li Efrînê ne, ez ji Efrînê me û ez zeytûnan pir
hez dikim.
 
Thank God we are in Afrin, I am from Afrin and I love olives
very much.

50
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Lê zeytûnên min nînin, min carekê jî zeytûn nedîtin, wê çima
wisa ye nizanim.
 
But I don't have olives, I haven't even seen olives once, I
don't know why it is like that.

51
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Metê Elî ye, Elî jî wekî bira ye.
 
It is Ali's aunt, Ali is also like a brother.

52
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Elî li Heleb dimîne, xeberek da min got em ê zeytûnên xwe
jêkin.
 
Ali lives in Aleppo, he sent me a message saying we will
pick our olives.

53
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Min got em ê herin.
 
I said we will go.

54
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Em va ye îro hatin.
 
Here we came today.

55
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Me ku ajotera xeber da ye, sê-çar gazî kirin, me got mazot
qut e.
 
When we informed the driver, called him three or four times,
we said the diesel is cut off.

56
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Mazot jî nebe, ekî çûbe çetin e.
 
If there is no diesel, if it's gone, it's difficult.

57
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Ekî çûbû, birê em ê bimeşin biftilin.
 
If it was gone, man, we will walk and turn back.

58
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Bi meşê.
 
By walking.

59
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Welleh me dil heye em motorên xwe bikirin.
 
By God, we have a desire to buy our motorcycles.

60
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Lê ez vî wextî ku em werin derve... xilas e.
 
But when we come outside at this time... it's over.

61
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Ev nav zeytûnên deşta gundê Selo ne.
 
These are among the olives of the Selo village plains.

62
00:04:49,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Ev perçe jî li deşta gundê Selo ye.
 
This piece of land is also on the Selo village plains.

63
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Lê lê lê, lê lê lê, lê lê lê, lê lê lê.
 
Le le le, le le le, le le le, le le le.

64
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
Ev zeytûn in ketine, yan te jêkirine?
 
Have these olives fallen, or did you pick them?

65
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Adeten ez vana wek perçên...
 
Usually I treat these like pieces of...

66
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Bes e...
 
Enough...

67
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Elî kanî? Elî fena tu dibêjî.
 
Where is Ali? Ali is like you say.

68
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
Tê fena xwe jêk bikî...
 
You will pick it your way...

69
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Na tu wisa...
 
No, you do it like that...

70
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Fena wê jêk bike...
 
Pick it its way...

71
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:56,000
Silavên min ji kekê Muhemmed û kekê Şukrî li derveyî welat
li Ewropayê re.
 
My greetings to brother Muhammed and brother Shukri abroad
in Europe.

72
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Xwedanê vê erdê, silavên me pir germ in ji kekê Muhemmed re.
 
The owner of this land, our greetings are very warm to
brother Muhammed.

73
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Xwedê te ke û emrê te dirêj be.
 
May God bless you and may your life be long.

74
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Û quwet bide canê we, bi taybetî.
 
And give strength to your soul, especially.

75
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Bi taybetî ku em îro hatin nav zeytûnan, darên we, em
qehweyekê vedixwin.
 
Especially since we came among the olives today, your trees,
we are drinking a coffee.

76
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Em li gund bûn, me xwest em vê vîdyoyê teswîr bikin.
 
We were in the village, we wanted to film this video.

77
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Da hûn darên xwe bibînin.
 
So that you can see your trees.

78
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Xwedê heke emrê we dirêj be, xwedê rehma xwe li bav û kalên
we bike.
 
If God grants, may your lives be long, may God have mercy on
your parents and ancestors.

79
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Înşallah dengekî nêzîk, hûn jî werin di nav darên xwe de, di
nav milkê xwe de.
 
God willing, in a near future, you will also come among your
trees, in your property.

80
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Silavên me ji hemû xelkên Efrînê re.
 
Our greetings to all the people of Afrin.

81
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Berê yekî gotinê digot, dewlet wê biftile, û min jî got em ê
biftilin.
 
Before, someone used to say, the state will return, and I
also said we will return.

82
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Bes ma... wehşellah mezin e.
 
But indeed... mashallah it is big.

83
00:06:55,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Berî em reş bikin, rast e, wextî me got, em ê biftilin.
 
Before we blacken it, it is true, when we said, we will
return.

84
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Nawa te çi gotî Selo?
 
What did you say, Selo?

85
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Ez dibêjim înşelah dewlet wê dîsa biftile.
 
I say, God willing, the state will return again.

86
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Dosta te nîme, yara te nîme... dildarê te me...
 
I am not your friend, I am not your lover... I am your
beloved...

87
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Kî remdar kên û zînê. Em e... dostê gulbarîn e.
 
Who is wounded and alive. We are... friends of the falling
roses.

88
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Bêhna malan evdar e, piştî malan evdar e.
 
The scent of the houses is fragrant, behind the houses it is
fragrant.

89
00:07:54,000 --> 00:08:12,000
Bi baxçe ye û bi hinar e, bi baxçe û bi hinar e.
 
With gardens and with pomegranates, with gardens and with
pomegranates.

90
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Tirba bavê wê li Urfê ye, tirba bavê wê li Urfê ye.
 
Her father's tomb is in Urfa, her father's tomb is in Urfa.

91
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:44,000
Me ra dixe wêran e... li Urfê li Urfê şêrîn Urfê.
 
It leaves us in ruins... in Urfa, in Urfa, sweet Urfa.

92
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Çol û ser xanî me de meşî... Xaniyê kul û ox de weşî...
 
In the fields and on our houses you walked... The house of
sorrow and sighs you shook...

93
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Lê lê rindamin. Qabik şikiyê da kef hewşê... Lê lê rindamin.
 
Oh, my beautiful one. The cup broke, scattering in the
courtyard... Oh, my beautiful one.

94
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Niha jî me dixwest em qehweya xwe di vê sibê de vexwin.
 
Now we also wanted to drink our coffee this morning.

95
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Ev qehweya ku dîn e em ê li nav zeytûnan vexwin.
 
We will drink this crazy coffee among the olive trees.

96
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Elî camêr bi xwe hosta ye, ew ê qehwê çêke.
 
Ali himself is a gentleman and a master, he will make the
coffee.

97
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Li min dinêre, bi dizîkî ve.
 
He looks at me, secretly.

98
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,000
Qehwê çawa çêdike... min dixwest ez wî bidim dîtin.
 
How he makes the coffee... I wanted to show him.

99
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Demek di vê jiyanê de em her tiştî dizanin, û em ji Efrînê
ne...
 
In a way, in this life we know everything, and we are from
Afrin...

100
00:09:56,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Em tu carî asilê xwe ji bîr nakin û înkar nakin.
 
We never forget our origin and we do not deny it.

101
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Ez ji Efrînê me, haçî me zeytûn e, haçî me Efrîn e, me
zeytûn dîtine na.
 
I am from Afrin, for us it's olive, for us it's Afrin, we
have seen olives.

102
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Lê bawer kin, malbateke rastî çavên wê li zeytûn e, xalê
Evdo, xalê Zekî, silavên me pir ji wê malbatê re heye.
 
But believe me, truly a family whose eyes are on the olives,
Uncle Evdo, Uncle Zeki, we send many greetings to that
family.

103
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Belkî em rojek bibin dîsa gidî li me bixwaze em zeytûnan
weke wê malbatê em herin.
 
Maybe one day they will invite us again to harvest olives
with that family.

104
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Em digiştin nav zeytûnan şore me re dikirin berî giya.
 
When we reached the olive fields, they would give us advice
before anything.

105
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Digotin wa ye şor kir li vir bisekinin.
 
They would say, 'Here they shook it, stay here'.

106
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Mîla şorê wa we ra narîne hawa yek e. Û ya didoyan ji,
 
Their advice was not in vain, that's one. And secondly,

107
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Digotin çawa mekin zeytûn me zîqariyan tê de derbaz kirin.
 
They would tell us what to do to get the olives through the
sieves.

108
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Wê tiştekî sîsê jî, muamele xwe pir ji me re rind bû,
 
And thirdly, their treatment of us was very good,

109
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Digot em digihiştin nav zeytûnan, sibehekê, helawê di me de,
digot ser silavê me bixwin,
 
They said when we arrived at the olive trees in the morning,
they gave us halva, saying 'eat to our health',

110
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Încax rehet bixwin... paşê qehwe çêdikirin,
 
'So you can eat comfortably'... then they would make coffee,

111
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Pir qîmetî me zanîn. Silavê me ji wê malbatê re heye, wexta
me pir nanê gêndixwariyê û şîvê me dixwest nav zeytûnan me
re çêdikirin...
 
We really appreciated it. We send our greetings to that
family, when we wanted a lot of food and dinner, they would
make it for us among the olive trees...

112
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Û ehbab û nas, ne xerîb û ne nas, gundî badînan, silavê me
pir ji wan re heye, xweda emrê wan dirêj bike.
 
And friends and acquaintances, neither strangers nor
acquaintances, the villagers of Badinan, we send many
greetings to them, may God give them a long life.

113
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
Û qesr nêta wa bide. Lew nêta wa pir paqij e...
 
And may their intentions be rewarded. Because their
intentions are very pure...

114
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:57,000
Û qîmetî wa di cîya ma û duayê ma ji wan re dikirin heta
naha ma wê rojê ji bîr nekiriye.
 
And we valued them in our place and we prayed for them, even
now we haven't forgotten that day.

115
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:02,000
De bi me re werin, em qehweyê vexwin.
 
Come with us, let's drink coffee.

116
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:05,000
Bimêş, bimêş, bimêş, bimêş
 
Walk, walk, walk, walk

117
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Lê lê, lê lê, rinda min
 
Oh, oh, my beautiful

118
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:11,000
Lê Sîno, lê Sîna min
 
Oh Sino, oh my Sina

119
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
Destmalekî çar qelem e
 
A four-colored handkerchief

120
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,000
Lê Sîno, lê Sîna min
 
Oh Sino, oh my Sina

121
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:18,000
Destmalekî çar qelem e
 
A four-colored handkerchief

122
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Lo bera ez ke bimrim
 
Oh let me just die

123
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Ji bo xatirê malxem e
 
For the sake of the beloved

124
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:26,000
Lê Sîno lê Sîna min
 
Oh Sino, oh my Sina

125
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:29,000
Destmalek çar qelem e
 
A four-colored handkerchief

126
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Lê Sîno lê Sîna min
 
Oh Sino, oh my Sina

127
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Destmalek çar qelem e
 
A four-colored handkerchief

128
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Lo bera ez ke bimrim
 
Oh let me just die

129
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
Ji bo xatirê malxem e
 
For the sake of the beloved

130
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Lo bera ez ke bimrim
 
Oh let me just die

