Yes. Now can you tell us... the price of the ladders, my
uncle..

239
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Her yeke yek mîşekil e.
 
Each one is a different size.

240
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Sî û dudû ye, sî û sê ye, bîst û heşt e...
 
It is 32, it is 33, it is 28...

241
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:43,000
Yê mezin e.. heye sî.. sî û pênc e, heta bîst û heşt... ev
ji Tirkîyê tê...
 
The big ones.. there's 30.. 35, up to 28... this comes from
Turkey...

242
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Bi dolar e.
 
It's in dollars.

243
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,000
Dolar.
 
Dollars.

244
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Ji sî û pênc a heta bîst û heşt a tê.
 
It goes from 35 down to 28.

245
00:18:47,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Belê, em tînin bi sî û pênc dolar a.. em difiroşin..
 
Yes, we bring it for 35 dollars.. we sell it..

246
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Ji sî û pênc e da dadikeve heta bîst û heşt a.
 
From 35 it drops down to 28.

247
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

248
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:27,000
Kar heye daxwazek heye, nexweşî tune masref û hwd heye...
 
There's work, there's demand, there's no problem, there are
expenses etc...

249
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Masref giran e... Kehreb a hebî...
 
Expenses are heavy... There is electricity...

250
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Nav ma wuzot dî baha kêm bî o tu çiqas mesref dikî j bo ve
tişta?
 
The price of diesel is high, so how much do you spend on
this?

251
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Here, her tişt me mesref zêde kr...
 
Yes, everything increased our expenses...

252
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Her tişt ser me diha giran tê...
 
Everything is more expensive for us...

253
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Noka mazot qet nîne gava ku em tînin jî biha ye wekî tu
dibînî...
 
Now diesel is completely gone, and when we bring it, it is
expensive, as you see...

254
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:57,000
Em dixwazin kar bikin lê gava mazot biha bibe em nikarin...
xelk jî nikarin bikirin.
 
We want to work but when diesel gets expensive we can't...
people can't buy it either.

255
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Dê ve mîntîqê Kîtîx da çend kesan ev kargeha silima vekir?
 
In this Kitix region, how many people opened this ladder
factory?

256
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Ez pênç şeş desta ma wa he.
 
We have five or six workshops.

257
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Xwedê xêr û bereket têxe vê kargehê.
 
May God bring goodness and blessing to this workshop.

258
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:27,000
Paşê me dest pê kir.
 
Then we started.

259
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Paşê koka, paçek koka me dît û te dest pê kir.
 
Then the root, we found a piece of root and you started.

260
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:51,000
Înge çêdikin nu, înge çêdikin ha.
 
They make rolling pins now, they make rolling pins.

261
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,000
Saatê we xweş, xalet.
 
Bless your time, aunt.

262
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Yê te jî pirkî xweş bî, xwedê ji te razî bî.
 
May yours be very pleasant too, may God be pleased with you.

263
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Amîn.
 
Amen.

264
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

265
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:20,000
Xaltiya min ev çêkirina kerte, çi qas wext ji te digire? Ji
destpêkê heta tu xilas dikî?
 
My aunt, making this carved tool, how much time does it take
you? From the beginning until you finish?

266
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:40,000
Ê wele wî roja teva ez çêdikim ser de rûdinim naqede.
 
Well, I make it the whole day, sit working on it, and it
doesn't finish.

267
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:51,000
Em mezin bûn li vî gundî
 
We grew up in this village

268
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:53,000
Her tiştê xwaş me tê dîdî
 
We saw everything beautiful in it

269
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:56,000
Çi xwaş sal çû umrê me çû
 
What a nice year passed, our life passed

270
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:58,000
Me nizanî ça derbas bû
 
We didn't know how it passed

271
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:01,000
Hîn ber çav in rûyên şêrîn
 
The sweet faces are still before our eyes

272
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:03,000
Digirîn ji wan wextên şêrîn
 
We cry from those sweet times

273
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Çi xweş bû zemanê şahî
 
How beautiful was the time of joy

274
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:08,000
Çîrokên tijî bi evîn
 
Stories full of love

275
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:11,000
Hey lê bala min
 
Oh, my mind

276
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:14,000
Şevên xas û bi rûşadî bûn
 
The special nights were full of joy

277
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:16,000
Dengê dîkan ra şiyar dibûn
 
They woke up to the sound of roosters

278
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:18,000
Azana sibê ra radibûn
 
They woke up to the morning adhan

279
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Her kes karî şixulê xwe bûn
 
Everyone was minding their own business

280
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:23,000
Qîz û law derve kom dibûn
 
Girls and boys would gather outside

281
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:26,000
Bi ken û rûyek xweş radibûn
 
They would get up with smiles and cheerful faces

282
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:28,000
Şivan e kar û berx dajo
 
The shepherd drives the kids and lambs

283
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:31,000
Heval bûn xwişk û bira bûn
 
We were friends, sisters and brothers

284
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:34,000
Hey lê bala min
 
Oh, my mind

285
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:36,000
Rojên gundê min
 
The days of my village

286
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:38,000
Hîn ber çavê min
 
Are still before my eyes

287
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Şevên gundê min
 
The nights of my village

288
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Nanê genimî tendûr da
 
Wheat bread in the tandoor

289
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:08,000
Dûmana şîn ji derikê dûr da
 
Blue smoke coming from the distant chimney

290
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:11,000
Digeriyan nava çol û sirta
 
They wandered in the deserts and ridges

291
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:13,000
Mexel dihatin pozê zinara
 
They came to rest at the peak of the rocks

292
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:16,000
Dest ne didan lîstîkê çokan
 
They didn't play games on their knees

293
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:18,000
Keçik dihatin kefa kaniyan
 
Girls came to the foam of the springs

294
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:21,000
Me vedixwar ji ava curnan
 
We drank from the water of the troughs

295
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:26,000
Te digot qey em teyrê ezmanan
 
You'd think we were the birds of the sky

296
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:28,000
Dengê xwendina zarokan
 
The sound of children reading

297
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Mekteb ava dibû nav gundan
 
School was built in the villages

298
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:33,000
Rûgeş dibûn dayîk û bavan
 
Mothers and fathers became joyful

299
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Dixemilîn wek malên zavan
 
They were adorned like the grooms' houses

300
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:38,000
Gunguma def û zurnan
 
The echoing of drums and zurnas

301
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:41,000
Govend girtin der û cîran
 
Neighbors and those around danced the govend

302
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Şekir reşandin ser serê bûkan
 
Sugar was sprinkled on the brides' heads

303
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:49,000
Hey lê bala min
 
Oh, my mind

304
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Ew hevalê min
 
That friend of mine

305
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:54,000
Narê ji bîra min
 
Doesn't leave my mind

306
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:59,000
Biçûktiya min
 
My childhood

